fact WorkItem(id: "WI-437", description: some(value: "anthill-todo: PLUGGABLE BACKEND -- per-project work-item data source selection (examples/github-todo/docs/pluggable-backend.md; the multi-developer driver: git conflicts in workitems.anthill). Project config selects one of: local (files, today's IndexedFileStore via the WI-009 SingleFile convention), github (work items are GitHub issues), api (future standardized remote). Natural shape = the path-dependent-types design sec.5 factory: openStore(cfg) -> C ensures Store[C, ...] returning local/github/api behind one store interface -- THE first real consumer of WI-402's existential half (ensures Spec[C] + dict-out), which is parked on this ticket for exactly that reason. Builds on the delivered WI-009 cutover (backend selection lives in the bundle's store layer; WorkItemStore spec already separates spec from FileBasedWorkitemStore impl). NOTE from the 2026-06-11 WI-200 analysis: multi-instance Modify state (WI-200) is NOT needed for the CLI path -- one backend instance per invocation, distinct backend SORTS occupy distinct slots, and the bundle state rides Cell (per-allocation arena identity); WI-200 becomes relevant only for the api/server direction (many stores in one process)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-009", "WI-402", "WI-699", "WI-830", "WI-1113", "WI-1114", "WI-1117", "WI-1118", "WI-1120", "WI-1121"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-437", author: "user", content: "DESIGN DOC (2026-07-12): rustland/anthill-todo/docs/design/backend-github-coordination.md is the full specification (supersedes examples/github-todo/docs/pluggable-backend.md). Key decisions: (1) stake-by-creation allocation, section 6.1 -- claims are staked by CREATING the issue already titled WI-<n>: (creation is atomic and totally ordered by issue number, so lowest-number-wins is sound); the earlier stake-by-retitle CAS had an unfixable both-keep interleaving. Registry reads use the issues LIST endpoint with --state all (the search index serves only the old-claimant leg); claims parsed strictly as ^WI-<n>: title prefix. (2) Autonomous mode, section 6.4 -- offline/unauth add mints a provisional WI-t<6hex> id from host entropy; sync reconciles (allocate permanent id, rename file, rewrite depends_on references); GithubAccess fact = project-wide default with per-checkout override (ANTHILL_TODO_GITHUB / --offline). (3) Full-backfill migration, section 11 -- every item mirrored including terminal ones (created-then-closed) so open/closed on GitHub reflects the whole tracker. (4) Return channels: section 7.3 issue comments ingest as Feedback facts (author github:<login>, ingest-once keyed (workitem, author, at), monotone-compatible; sync-authored comments carry an [anthill-todo sync] marker and are skipped); section 7.4 closing a Delivered item issue = verify GESTURE, event-not-state (close in any other state = drift: reopened + reported; reopen of terminal = drift). Governing principle: every datum has exactly ONE writable home. (5) Mirror is a CARRIER sort (authority = possession; gh-backed and fake implementations injected at the WI-402 factory), NOT a new effect; its ops ride the generic External effect -- hence the added dependency on WI-698 (proposal docs/proposals/054-external-effect.md); spec rows for alloc_id/commit become {Modify[s], External, Error}. (6) Forge-substitution contract, section 8.3 -- GitHub is one carrier implementation; a substitute must provide: atomic creation totally ordered by identifier, live newest-first listing with current titles and state, title search reaching arbitrarily old entries, comments with stable (author, created_at), and entries that persist once created. Increments (section 14, substrate-first): 1 store-factory seam (single bare spec-op call: stamp_format at main.anthill:2837), 2 StateDirs + relocation rule + fsck, 3 External (WI-698) + Mirror carrier + fake, 4 coordinated add + provisional fallback, 5 sync (reconcile / ingest / close-as-verify / push / tombstones), 6 migrate. Related: WI-697 (timeout autoverify -- the fully-autonomous sibling of section 7.4).", at: "2026-07-12T07:38:55Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-437", author: "user", content: "DESIGN DOC POINTER, refreshed (2026-07-12, post-push). The full specification is rustland/anthill-todo/docs/design/backend-github-coordination.md, now COMMITTED AND PUSHED in 890e1399 -- it was still untracked when the earlier DESIGN DOC feedback was written. READ THIS FIRST: the DESCRIPTION of this item still cites examples/github-todo/docs/pluggable-backend.md, which is SUPERSEDED; backend-github-coordination.md is the current spec. Increments are its section 14: (1) store-factory substrate, (2) StateDirs + fsck, (3) Mirror capability + fake, (4) coordinated add + provisional ids, (5) sync (reconcile / repair / push / tombstone), (6) migrate. DEPENDENCY REWIRE (same session): this item used to depend on WI-698; WI-698 was split into an umbrella plus children, and the edge now points at WI-699 -- declare the generic External effect -- which is the ENTIRE critical path to increment 3, whose Mirror carrier ops need the {External, Error} rows. The hardening gates (WI-700 row conformance at explicit instantiation, WI-701 Branch x External, WI-702 purity-consumer gates) are NOT on this path and must not be re-added as blockers on this item. The effect design is proposal 054 (docs/proposals/054-external-effect.md); its section Mechanism carries the ER/EW carrier-tied row-param split that section 8.3 of the design doc relies on.", at: "2026-07-12T11:28:04Z")

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-437", name: "wi437")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-437", author: "user", content: "SPLIT 2026-08-16 into an umbrella plus six children, one per section-14 increment, on the WI-698 -> WI-699..703 precedent: WI-1113 store-factory substrate, WI-1114 state directories, WI-1115 Mirror carrier + fake, WI-1116 coordinated add, WI-1117 sync, WI-1118 migrate (tag: wi437). Each is stated by the design to be independently green and independently useful, and this item as one ticket could not be claimed and delivered atomically. THIS ITEM IS NOW THE UMBRELLA -- it depends on all six and delivers when they do; do not claim it. Chain: 1 gates 2 and 3, which together gate 4, then 5, then 6.\n\nWHAT THE SPLIT SURFACED, and it is increment 1's first job: THE DESIGN DOC HAS DRIFTED AT ITS OWN SUBSTRATE. Section 3 specifies 'fact StoreBackend(kind: BackendKind)' in project.anthill as the configuration channel. It was written 2026-07-12; WI-830 landed on 2026-08-16 and put 'fact ExtentBinding(store:, role:, covers:)' in that same file doing that same job -- the project declares a store term, the host maps it to a compiled-in backend -- plus role and coverage. Adding StoreBackend beside it would give one datum two writable homes, which is the failure section 7's governing principle exists to prevent. The reconciliation is that BackendKind's config rides ExtentBinding.store as an applied term: a GithubCoordinatedStore(repo:, root:, project:, access:) slots exactly where IndexedFileStore(root:, convention:) sits today. What remains of section 8.2's open_store existential under that reading is the open question increment 1 answers, and the amendment lands as its own commit before any code.\n\nVERIFIED STILL-OPEN, section 14 row 1 (checked against the tree at e3120429): 'store: FileStore' is still threaded through main/dispatch and every cmd_*, passed at 16 sites, and NO body in main.anthill calls persist/retract/flush on it -- so section 8.2's claim that it is vestigial and a pure deletion holds. The one bare spec-op call site is likewise still bare, but at main.anthill:3184; section 8.2's citation of :2837 is stale and increment 1 fixes it.", at: "2026-08-16T10:48:09Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-437", author: "user", content: "CHAIN AMENDED 2026-08-16: seven children, not six. WI-1120 was inserted between increments 2 and 3 -- \"work items are documents\", the declared fact<->markdown mapping (design §5.3). It depends on WI-1114 and BLOCKS WI-1118, because the live tracker migrates exactly once and must migrate into the final on-disk format; settling the format after the migration would mean migrating twice. Chain now: 1 gates 2 and 3; 2 gates 2b; 2 and 3 together gate 4; then 5; then 6, which additionally waits on 2b. The earlier feedback note on this item describing \"an umbrella plus six children\" predates the insertion.", at: "2026-08-16T17:32:35Z")
